    "package": {
      "title": "6105 Final Shaving Accommodation (Officer)",
      "description": "Final 6105 counseling at twelve months of clean-shaven medical accommodation for a Marine officer: MEB referral, AA Form extension request, separation under SECNAVINST 1920.6D encl (3) para 3005 with RE-3P (the counseling MARADMIN 348/26 para 3.b.3.a requires; wording per MARADMIN 192/26).",
      "documentType": "page11"
    }
  },
  "data": {
    "formData": {
      "documentType": "page11",
      "name": "",
      "edipi": "",
      "date": "",
      "remarksLeft": "[YYYYMMDD]: Counseled this date concerning the following deficiencies: inability to comply with clean-shaven grooming standards established in MCO 1020.34H and having reached 12 consecutive months of treatment requiring a medical accommodation.\n\nThe accommodation was approved by the commanding officer on [YYYYMMDD] and documented on NAVMC 11830. The accommodation will expire [YYYYMMDD], which is twelve months from the date of approval.\n\nMarine Officers requiring clean-shaven grooming accommodations due to a medical condition for more than twelve months will be evaluated for administrative separation under SECNAVINST 1920.6D (Administrative Separation of Officers), Enclosure (3), paragraph 3005 (Physical Condition Not Constituting a Disability) and if separated will be assigned a reentry code of RE-3P.\n\nGrooming Standards: You must strictly maintain facial hair length not to exceed one quarter of an inch (0.25) in length.\n\nSpecific recommendations for corrective action are to continue to comply fully with the prescribed medical treatment plan, to attend all scheduled medical evaluations and re-evaluations as appropriate.\n\nUnderstand that you will receive a formal referral to a Medical Evaluation Board (MEB) to document whether your condition constitutes a physical disability under the Disability Evaluation System (DES).\n\nYou must submit an Administrative Action Form (NAVMC 10274) requesting an administrative extension to your clean-shaven accommodation while the MEB and separation proceedings are pending. You shall carry a copy of your expired NAVMC 11830 along with a copy of your submitted AA Form or the approved DC M&RA extension at all times and present if requested.\n\nI understand that failure to complete my service obligation with an honorable characterization of service may preclude my eligibility for benefits from the Department of Veterans Affairs or other organizations and have an adverse effect on future civilian employment.\n\nI was advised that within 5 working days after acknowledging this entry I may submit a written rebuttal which will be filed in the electronic service record. I choose to ____ / not to ____ make such a statement.\n\n\n______________________________\nSignature of Marine Officer\n\n\n______________________________\nSignature of Commanding Officer",
      "remarksRight": ""
    },
    "vias": [],
